{"id": "EUVD-2026-41498", "enisaUuid": "4ff4ed70-939d-34db-8ebc-be08d105f326", "description": "An issue in curl\u2019s QUIC UDP receive function allows a malicious HTTP/3 server\nto trigger a remote denial of service against a curl or libcurl client.\nBecause the helper function discards zero-length UDP datagrams before counting\nthem toward the per-call packet budget, a connected QUIC peer can continuously\nstream empty datagrams to indefinitely stall the client.", "datePublished": "2026-07-03T06:12:10", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-15T06:02:38", "baseScore": 7.5, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H", "references": ["https://curl.se/docs/CVE-2026-11352.json", "https://curl.se/docs/CVE-2026-11352.html", "https://hackerone.com/reports/3783438"], "aliases": ["GHSA-qxwx-hr5v-h5q4", "CVE-2026-11352"], "assigner": "curl", "epss": 0.72, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "18cc038d-e63f-34ba-b04b-3b59f6814227", "product": {"name": "curl", "vendor": {"name": "curl"}}, "product_version": "8.20.0"}, {"id": "44b25edb-6961-3509-a28f-9f5ea9f4ba85", "product": {"name": "curl", "vendor": {"name": "curl"}}, "product_version": "6a3d0b6d631d5e9bec797306b5b41a9f440a088d <56eca2afb4806f1032872fa97d1834b3c1385276"}, {"id": "44ffff5a-f36f-3b03-aa56-433ceec54ab0", "product": {"name": "curl", "vendor": {"name": "curl"}}, "product_version": "8.18.0 <8.20.1"}, {"id": "a189350c-3b69-3ca8-9068-ac6a34e1c838", "product": {"name": "curl", "vendor": {"name": "curl"}}, "product_version": "8.19.0"}, {"id": "a40f0ac6-6081-3894-bdf3-4807c035e837", "product": {"name": "curl", "vendor": {"name": "curl"}}, "product_version": "8.18.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "50ef7200-9242-3e78-bc83-be0826506e4e", "vendor": {"name": "curl"}}], "isExploited": false}